54e6211c","at":"2026-09-27T15:20:33.728Z","channel":"system","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"design-agent","name":"Design agent (Recorded run · Claude Opus 5.5 · Sep 26)","channel":"system"},"kind":"message","text":"[Recorded run · Claude Opus 5.5 · Sep 26] I've drawn up revision 1 of your Moon-Phase Lamp. Three of the five checks pass, but the other two couldn't run, so I haven't released it.\n\n**The design**\n- **Lights:** four yellow lights in a row on pins D2–D5 (the Arduino's numbered connection points). Each light has a 220 Ω resistor, which limits the current so the light and the board stay safe.\n- **Phases:** the lamp starts at full moon. Each button press moves one step through the 8 moon phases: new moon (no lights), then growing from the right (1, 2, 3 lights), full moon (all 4), then shrinking from the right (3, 2, 1 lights), then back to new moon.\n- **Button:** on pin D7. It counts each press once, even if you hold it down.\n- **Dark sensor:** the light sensor is paired with the 10 kΩ resistor and read on pin A0. The lamp turns on when the reading drops below 300 (dark) and turns off above 340 (bright). The gap between the two numbers stops it flickering at dusk. At the bench, ViBread measures your room and adjusts both numbers.\n- **In a bright room:** the button still moves the phase forward. You'll see the new phase once it gets dark.\n\n**Check results**\n- Electrical: **GO.** Each pin carries at most about 16 mA (the limit is 20 mA), and the whole circuit draws about 64 mA.\n- Firmware (the program for the board): **GO.** It compiles, and the pin settings match the wiring.\n- Breadboard layout: **GO.** Everything fits, and the placed wires match the design.\n- Simulation tests: **not run.** An independent writer has to create these tests, and ViBread needs a connected Claude account to do that. The server says it isn't connected.\n- Independent review: **not run.** It only starts once every other check is GO.\n\n**Assumptions to check**\n- \"Next day's phase\" is simplified to the next of 8 phases per press, because four lights can only show 8 distinct shapes.\n- The moon is shown as seen from the northern hemisphere, so it grows and shrinks from the right.\n- The lamp doesn't ","data":{"recorded":{"label":"Recorded run · Claude Opus 5.5 · Sep 26","model":"claude-opus-5-5","recordedAt":"2026-09-26T10:08:58-05:00"}}},{"id":"c83415f9-74f8-4b80-9617-bc0bd07bca5e","missionId":"e45466e6-032c-4325-b85f-906d54e6211c","at":"2026-09-27T15:20:33.730Z","channel":"system","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"test-author","name":"Independent test author (Recorded run · Claude Sonnet 5 · Sep 26)","channel":"system"},"kind":"revision.created","text":"Revision 2: revision 1 with 8 independent simulation tests (Recorded run · Claude Sonnet 5 · Sep 26)","revision":2,"data":{"hash":"14cd9fc71217d85da8d4c0107562e749bbab439261825c7bd2558fef4aef4ed7","parent":1,"recorded":{"label":"Recorded run · Claude Sonnet 5 · Sep 26","model":"claude-sonnet-5","recordedAt":"2026-09-26T10:12:00-05:00"}}},{"id":"a541a1c5-a35c-47eb-881d-ca76fe74e79f","missionId":"e45466e6-032c-4325-b85f-906d54e6211c","at":"2026-09-27T15:20:35.788Z","channel":"system","actor":{"kind":"system","id":"pipeline","name":"ViBread checks","channel":"system"},"kind":"console.report","text":"Electrical checks (EECOM): GO — All electrical checks pass.","revision":2,"data":{"console":"EECOM","verdict":"GO","errors":0,"timings":{"compile":0,"eecom":2,"assemblyLoad":40,"layout":131,"pinModes":173,"fao":2,"steps":6,"breadboardSvg":57,"selftest":65,"spice":540,"schematic":394,"stepImages":1290,"sim":2050,"guido":1,"benchFirmware":1818,"total":2057}}},{"id":"5bcebb0a-5594-4373-822c-653bf4d54ec9","missionId":"e45466e6-032c-4325-b85f-906d54e6211c","at":"2026-09-27T15:20:35.789Z","channel":"system","actor":{"kind":"system","id":"pipeline","name":"ViBread checks","channel":"system"},"kind":"console.report","text":"Firmware (GUIDO): GO — All firmware checks pass.","revision":2,"data":{"cons